<title>USA: U.S. factory vegoil product use - Census.</title>
<headline>U.S. factory vegoil product use - Census.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. factories used 1,311.2 million lbs of vegoils in April in edible product output versus a revised 1,127.3 million lbs in March and 1,213.2 in April 1996.</p>
<p>U.S. factory vegoil use with refining losses were as follows:</p>
<p>   (Mln Lbs) --  April 97  March 97   April 96</p>
<p>    Soybean Oil   1,080.6   1,137.6   1,035.2</p>
<p> Cottonseed Oil	N/A	N/A	    N/A</p>
<p>Year-to-date oil use with refining losses (Mln Lbs):</p>
<p>				    1997	   1996</p>
<p>		 Soybean Oil   4,344.5	4,091.1</p>
<p>	    Cottonseed Oil	 N/A	    N/A</p>
<p> OUTPUT -- Soybean Crude   5,175.5	5,148.1</p>
<p>		     Refined   3,977.7	3,954.2</p>
<p>	  Cottonseed Crude     457.0	  596.0</p>
<p>		     Refined     319.5	  347.3</p>
<p>		  Corn Crude     741.3	  726.1</p>
<p>		     Refined     274.3	  335.2</p>
</text>
